-## Website requirements
+## Eligibility and availability 
+
+### Website requirements
 
 If you’re based in the Netherlands, your website must comply with iDEAL | Wero scheme rules by clearly displaying your KVK (company registration) number with the Chamber of Commerce. If you aren’t based in the Netherlands, your website must display your registration number with the equivalent local official body.
 
-## Connect
+### Connect
 
-When using iDEAL | Wero with *Connect* (Connect is Stripe's solution for multi-party businesses, such as marketplace or software platforms, to route payments between sellers, customers, and other recipients), the connected account’s name must map to its actual business, not to the platform. This is important for regulatory compliance and customer trust, because customers will see this business name during the iDEAL | Wero payment flow.+When using iDEAL | Wero with *Connect* (Connect is Stripe's solution for multi-party businesses, such as marketplace or software platforms, to route payments between sellers, customers, and other recipients), the connected account’s name must map to its actual business, not to the platform. This is important for regulatory compliance and customer trust, because customers will see this business name during the iDEAL | Wero payment flow.
+
+### Prohibited business categories 
+
+In addition to the industry and business categories listed in [Prohibited and restricted businesses](https://stripe.com/restricted-businesses), the following categories are prohibited or restricted from using iDEAL | Wero:
+
+- Adult content, entertainment, and sex-related products and services
+- Cannabis businesses, excluding cannabidiol (CBD)
+- Non-fungible tokens (NFTs)
+- Payment facilitators that process payments for sub-merchants
+- Peer-to-peer money transfers
+- Contracts for difference (CFDs)
+- Weapons and firearms
+- Donation-based crowdfunding
+- Creator economy and live-streaming businesses
+- Open-loop gaming
+- Traders in precious metals or minerals
+- Any business whose activities are prohibited by applicable law or regulation, including terrorist financing, human trafficking, illegal narcotics dealing, and shell banks